# The build context is uploaded to Fly's builder on every deploy, so anything
# that is not needed to *run* the server is excluded. The single biggest win is
# data/ — 3.2 GB of database that belongs on the volume, not in the image.
data/
research/
progress/
automation/
.git/
.github/
.claude/
node_modules/

# Documentation and planning notes: ~200 KB of Markdown the server never reads.
*.MD
*.md

# The tests. The sweep and sync entrypoints do ship (COPY src/ takes the whole
# directory) — they are inert in the container, and excluding them one by one
# buys nothing but a list to forget to maintain.
src/*-test.mjs

# Secrets. On Fly the key arrives as a real environment variable (`fly secrets
# set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...`, see docs/deploy.md), which wins over a file
# anyway, so baking a local .env into the image would add nothing but a copy of
# the key.
.env
.env.local
config/

.DS_Store
npm-debug.log*
